<article class="env-remark" id="08A1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08A1">Remark <span data-tag="08A1">33.35.4</span>.</a> Let $k$ be an infinite field. Let $n \geq 1$. Given a finite number of coherent modules $\mathcal{F}_ i$ on $\mathbf{P}^ n_ k$ we can choose a single $s \in \Gamma (\mathbf{P}^ n_ k, \mathcal{O}(1))$ such that the statement of Lemma <a href="/tag/08A0" data-tag="08A0">33.35.3</a> works for each of them. To prove this, just apply the lemma to $\bigoplus \mathcal{F}_ i$. </p>
</article>